        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="caveat" value="⚠ Honest caveat (docs/SPEC_PIPELINE.md §The information barrier):&#10;This barrier is a documented convention enforced by each agent's frontmatter permission.read deny patterns. Live-fire testing found it holds under normal instruction, but is NOT reliably enforced under explicit user override — at least one of the four subagents (Architect) complied when told to ignore its scope and read 00-informal.md anyway. Treat the barrier as a strongly-worded convention backed by the stage-4 Verifier gate, not as a security boundary. The Verifier's scenario-traceability check (scripts/check-scenario-traceability.sh) is the actual behavioral enforcement — an agent that peeked and implemented something not in any scenario still fails the gate." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=5;fontSize=10" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="600" width="1020" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
